{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And she bore et Cain and said, etc.</b> The explanation follows the way of the masters of blessed memory (Zohar vol. 1, 54a): Cain is the aspect of evil and Abel is the aspect of good, and he is the soul of Moses our master, peace be upon him (Tikkun 69). Now, through the mediation of the excess of wounds that Cain inflicted upon Abel until he killed him — as they said of blessed memory (Sanhedrin 37b) that he did not know where the soul is located — thereby he removed the portion of evil from him, and the good was recognized as absolute. And this is the meaning of her saying <b>קָנִיתִי</b>, etc. — meaning, through this mediation: קָנִיתִי, a man who is Moses, אֶת HaShem. For this reality of being with HaShem as Moses, peace be upon him, was attained only through the mediation of the suffering that Cain inflicted upon him."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {0 "The abbreviation 'תיקון סט' refers to Tikkun 69 of the Tikkunei Zohar. The phrase 'באמצעות' (through the mediation of) governs the entire logical chain: the wounds mediated the removal of evil, which in turn mediated the attainment of Moses' level."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:39:02.110053027Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}